# Superstore Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

## 📊 Visualizations & Key Takeaways

### 1. Monthly & Quarterly Sales Trends
![Monthly Sales](monthly_sale.png)
![Quaterly_Sales](quaterly_sale.png)
* **Seasonal Pattern:** Sales remain flat during Q1/Q2, then rise sharply starting in August.
* **Peak Volume:** November and December consistently record the highest sales volume of the year due to holiday demand.
* **Business Insight:** Restock inventory 45–60 days prior to November to avoid stockouts during peak months.

---

### 2. Customer Demographics (Age Groups)
![Customer Age Groups](age_group.png)

* **Primary Segment:** The majority of customers fall within the **25–40** and **41–60** age brackets (working professionals).
* **Secondary Segment:** Customers under 25 and over 60 represent a significantly smaller portion of total orders.
* **Business Insight:** Tailor digital marketing campaigns toward working adults, focusing on high-value technology and home-office equipment.

---

### 3. Non-Obvious Insight: Discount vs. Profit Loss
![Discount vs Profit](profit_dis.png)

* **The Tipping Point:** Profit drops sharply into negative territory whenever discount rates exceed **20%**.
* **Profit Leakage:** Deep discounts generate higher sales volume but actively destroy net earnings.
* **Business Insight:** Implement a strict promotional discount cap of **15%–20%** across all product categories.
